From: Anthony Johnson <105193579+Johnson-Anthony@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:27:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] recorders: add camss_ir reader for the Surface Laptop 7
 IR camera

The ST VD55G0 IR sensor sits behind Qualcomm CAMSS, whose raw video node needs
media links and formats configured before streaming, and its IR flood LED is fired
by the sensor's own strobe output (V4L2 control led_mode). Stream GREY frames
through v4l2-ctl with manual exposure, restart once on a stalled stream, and stop
the stream (and so the strobe) if the Howdy process dies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
